                                                         "text":  "[AUD-CC-005] Strategic coherence (Rumelt): stated priorities (compile-speed MOAT, self-hosting, launch readiness) do not align with defect mass - launch/marketing surfaces are broken and flagship MOAT claims are unsubstantiated while compiler internals are comparatively healthy -- Single synthesis finding: across the 101-finding set, the deepest recent investment (v1.25-v1.39: generics, self-host ports, perf, bootstrap gate) matches stated MOAT priorities and shows health (AUD-LMAS-NEG clean T-number traceability, AUD-FT-008 zero undocumented unwrap violations, verified-real 37-subcommand surface), yet \u0027launch readiness\u0027 is contradicted by the outermost funnel: install paths 404 (PR-006), primary conversion CTAs dead (AM-001/CI-001), README status table broken markdown (PR-005), benchmarks evidence surface internally inconsistent 7-vs-6 (CI-003), release artifacts unsigned (CICD-004). The marketed MOAT itself is overclaimed: README/website present-tense Rayon+GPU dispatch vs book admissions it is not wired end-to-end (CI-002, CI-006), T1 panic hook dead (CC-002), quality gates advisory despite \u0027hard gate\u0027 prose (TC-005, CICD-008). This is systematic drift: internal capability outran external truth-in-marketing and funnel hardening."
