                                         "message":  {
                                                         "text":  "[AUD-FT-006] Kernelspec advertises interrupt_mode=\u0027signal\u0027 but the kernel has no SIGINT handler - interrupt kills the kernel -- KERNEL_INTERRUPT_MODE = \"signal\" (kernelspec.rs:50) tells Jupyter to interrupt via SIGINT (Unix) / CTRL_BREAK_EVENT (Windows). The Rust kernel process installs no signal handler (grep \u0027interrupt|SIGINT\u0027 in buff-jupyter/src: only the ACK-only interrupt_request at kernel.rs:250-255, documented as \u0027ack only, cancellation lands in T129c+\u0027). With the OS default disposition, that signal terminates the whole kernel process - so \u0027Interrupt kernel\u0027 in Jupyter kills the session (losing all cross-cell state) rather than stopping the running cell."
