                                                           }
                                                       ]
                                     },
                                     {
                                         "message":  {
                                                         "text":  "[AUD-PRIV-002] ~/.buff/credentials bearer token written plaintext with no restrictive permissions -- save_credentials_to serializes the bearer token to TOML and writes it with plain fs::write (registry.rs:236-239); no 0600/ACL hardening. On Unix a default umask yields world-readable 0644. The docstring defers only atomicity (\u0027a future hardening pass can swap in a temp-file + rename\u0027), not permissions. Prior squads flagged this; it remains unhardened."
                                                     },
