                                     {
                                         "message":  {
                                                         "text":  "[AUD-RGD-003] GitHub OAuth architecture transfers personal data to GitHub Inc. (US) with no documented transfer basis -- OAuth constants hardwire GitHub endpoints (github.com/login/oauth/authorize, api.github.com/user). Login involves a third-country (US) processor: the user\u0027s GitHub identity (login + numeric id) is fetched from GitHub Inc. infrastructure and persisted locally. Data minimization is good - scope read:user only, no email/profile scopes, only two fields deserialized."
                                                     },
