                                                                                                             },
                                                                                        "region":  {
                                                                                                       "startLine":  1,
                                                                                                       "endLine":  178
                                                                                                   }
                                                                                    }
                                                           }
                                                       ]
                                     },
                                     {
                                         "message":  {
                                                         "text":  "[AUD-TC-003] Jupyter kernel protocol core (kernel.rs run loop + execution.rs) never driven by any test -- kernel.rs is the largest file in buff-jupyter (1,470 lines, 64KB) and exposes the entire kernel as `Kernel::new(transport, conn)` + `pub async fn run()` - the Jupyter message loop handling execute_request/execute_reply/iopub. The crate\u0027s 5 test files (connection_tests, hmac_tests, kernelspec_tests, kernel_info_tests, wire_tests; ~17KB total vs 175KB of src) import only the peripheral helpers: connection::ConnectionFile, hmac::{sign,verify}, kernelspec, messages::{KernelInfoReply, BANNER}, wire::{MessageHeader, WireMessage}. No test imports kernel::Kernel, calls run(), or performs an execute_request -\u003e execute_reply/status=iopub round-trip. execution.rs (10.5KB, cross-cell state) is likewise unreferenced. kernel.rs contains no inline #[cfg(test)] module either."
                                                     },
                                         "ruleId":  "BUFF-test-coverage",
                                         "level":  "error",
                                         "locations":  [
                                                           {
                                                               "physicalLocation":  {
                                                                                        "artifactLocation":  {
