                                                                                                   }
                                                                                    }
                                                           }
                                                       ]
                                     },
                                     {
                                         "message":  {
                                                         "text":  "[AUD-TC-006] Aggregate: 9 of 73 crates have no tests/ directory; buff-lang-ffi-guide has zero tests entirely; 23 crates carry no inline unit tests -- Census via Glob+Grep (73 crates): (a) 9 crates lack a tests/ dir and rely solely on inline #[cfg(test)]: buff-lang-ast-rsx (1 inline file), buff-lang-buffhtml-parser (3), buff-lang-check (2 files, 45 inline #[test] fns), buff-lang-ffi-guide (0 tests - docs-only crate, lib.rs is 19 lines), buff-lang-fmt (1), buff-lang-pipeline (12 inline matches across 5 src files incl. rustc_invoke.rs and error_mapper.rs), buff-mcp (3), buff-msgpack (1), buff-protobuf (1). (b) 23 crates (mostly framework waves) have a tests/ dir but no inline unit tests. (c) All 44 framework crates have at least one tests/*.rs file (verified per-crate counts; min=1). (d) Snapshot corpus: 285 .snap files across crates. Per CONTRIBUTING.md, integration tests belong in tests/ and inline modules are \u0027fine for unit smoke\u0027 - so (a) is a convention-drift signal, not a violation, EXCEPT buff-lang-pipeline and buff-lang-check, whose lib APIs (compile_rust_to_exe helpers, check_source) are critical-path and only smoke-tested inline; they are exercised indirectly via buff-lang-cli\u0027s 40 test files, which is the mitigating golden fallback that keeps this finding at medium rather than high."
                                                     },
