                                                                                                   }
                                                                                    }
                                                           }
                                                       ]
                                     },
                                     {
                                         "message":  {
                                                         "text":  "[AUD-TC-007] Tautological assertion: test asserts Ok(()) is_ok() with no behavioral content -- translation.rs line 313-316 (`dap_result_alias_compiles`) constructs `let ok: DapResult\u003c()\u003e = Ok(());` and asserts `ok.is_ok()`. The value is a literal Ok, so the assertion can never fail - the test only proves the type alias exists (which the compiler already proves by compiling). The same file\u0027s other tests are strong (message-content asserts, ordering asserts), making this an isolated weak spot. A workspace-wide tautology scan (assert!(true), assert_eq!(true,true), literal-Ok is_ok) found only this instance in crates/*/tests/ (one more inline instance exists at buff-eval/src/lib.rs:841, not context-verified)."
                                                     },
